# Text shown by the code (Loc.Get("Area.Name")): dialogue, objectives, the handbook, hints. {0}, {1}... are filled in by the code.
Text: {
	Bridge: {
		OnBeach: Use the blueprint standing on a beach, facing the sea.
		NoRoom: Too close to the edge of the world, or the sea is too shallow: the bridge won't fit here.
		NoSea: No sea within 60 tiles ahead. Use it facing the sea.
		OutOfWorld: The bridge would run past the edge of the world.
		Blocked: Something you built is in the bridge's way (near {0}, {1}). Clear it first, or pick another spot.
		AlreadyBuilt: This world already has the bridge.
		Outline: The blueprint shows the bridge's outline (in green). If it looks right, stay where you are and use the blueprint again to build it.
		Built: Tazuna's bridge stands. The bridge builder is waiting for you in the hut at its end.
	}

	Vow: {
		School: {
			None: none
			Sharingan: Sharingan
			EightGates: Eight Gates
			Byakugan: Byakugan · Gentle Fist
			Sage: Sage Arts · Nine-Tails
		}

		Chapter: {
			None: ""
			Sharingan: The Curse Mark
			EightGates: Training with Guy
			Byakugan: The Hyuga Main and Branch Houses
			Sage: Mount Myoboku
		}
	}

	Hiruzen: {
		Greeting1: (He breathes out a puff of smoke.) ...So you've come.
		Greeting2: Everyone in this village is my family. You too.
		Greeting3: The Will of Fire will always be passed on.
		Called:
			'''
			...You've come. Kakashi tells me you've reached the threshold of a path.

			Which path a ninja walks is theirs to decide. When you've made up your mind, wear that style's core and choose "Take a vow". Sage Arts can only be learned after the Destruction of the Leaf; if that is your path, you may wait.
			'''
		NoVow: You have not taken a vow yet. Once you have a style core, wear it and come to me.
		YourPath: Your ninja way: {0}.
		ButtonVow: Take a vow
		ButtonAbout: About styles
		NoCore:
			'''
			To take a vow, you need something to vow to. The first tier of every style core lies between the Chunin Exams and the Destruction of the Leaf: the Sharingan in the Forest of Death, the Byakugan with Neji, the Eight Gates in the fight with Gaara.

			Sage Arts come only after the Destruction of the Leaf; if that is your path, you may wait.

			When you have a core, wear it and come to me.
			'''
		AlreadyVowed: You vowed long ago: {0}. ...Walk it to the end.
		Vowed:
			'''
			...Very well. From today, {0} is your ninja way.

			The training that belongs to this path, "{1}", will find you in time. (This chapter is still in development.)

			Sage Arts come only after the Destruction of the Leaf. If you change your mind one day, come and see me again.
			'''
		NeedsFee:
			'''
			You want to leave {0} for {1}?

			You may. But it costs {2} gold; think of it as a gift toward the village's repairs. What you gained on the old path stays with you, but it will no longer work.

			If you are sure, choose "Take a vow" once more.
			'''
		CannotPay: Changing paths costs {0} gold. If you don't have it, save up first.
		Changed:
			'''
			...Very well. Set down {0} and walk the way of {1}.

			The training of "{2}" will find you in time.
			'''
		About:
			'''
			Styles are paths of training that cross every class, carried by style cores. Anyone may wear a core, one at a time, and use it with the [Style Technique] key.

			To take a vow is to choose one as your own ninja way. Then training that belongs to that path alone awaits you:
			- Sharingan — the Curse Mark    - Eight Gates — training with Guy
			- Byakugan — the Hyuga Main and Branch Houses    - Sage Arts — Mount Myoboku

			Sage Arts come only after the Destruction of the Leaf. You may change paths, but it has a price.
			'''
	}

	Anko: {
		HeardOrochimaru:
			'''
			...What did you say? Long hair, eyes like a snake?

			(Her hand goes to the back of her neck without her meaning it to.) ...Leave him to me. You just head for the tower. He's not someone you can handle.
			'''
		Rules:
			'''
			Well, well, another one come to die. I'm the proctor of the second test, Mitarashi Anko.

			The rules are simple: one scroll each, Heaven or Earth. Take the other kind from someone else and bring both to the central tower, deep in the forest. No time limit. Though the longer you stay in these woods, the likelier you end up as bug food.
			'''
		Hurry: Still dawdling here? The central tower is in the heart of the forest. ...Don't make me go in and fetch your body.
		NotYet: This is the second test. Brats who haven't passed the written test, keep out.
		Survived: You actually came out alive? ...Heh. Interesting.
		ButtonScroll: Take a scroll
		Issue:
			'''
			(She tosses you a scroll.) The {0}. Hang on to it.

			...And no peeking inside on the way, okay? People die doing that.
			'''
	}

	Hayate: {
		Prelims:
			'''
			(Cough.) ...I am the proctor of the preliminaries, Gekko Hayate.

			Too many of you passed the second test, so there will be a match here first. One on one, until one of you falls. ...Tell me when you are ready.
			'''
		Passed: (Cough.) ...Congratulations. The finals are a month away. Prepare well.
		NotYet: (Cough.) ...This is where the second test ends. Come back with both the Heaven and Earth Scrolls.
		ButtonStart: Begin the preliminaries
	}

	Exam: {
		WrittenPassed: First test passed ({0} of the first nine right, {1} silver earned). Second test: the Forest of Death. Collect your scroll at the gate of Training Ground 44 in the jungle.{2}
		GateSquad:
			'''
			A corner of a scroll shows in the fallen candidate's jacket: the {0}, the same as yours.
			Candidate: "...Hmph. Want the {1}? Try your luck near the tower... the Rain..."
			'''
		Vial: ...A vial rolls on the ground. Floating in it is a red eye.
		RainTrioDown: The Rain trio is down, and they carried just the scroll you were missing
		GotScroll: "{0}: you got the {1}! Bring both scrolls to the central tower in the middle of the jungle.{2}"
		PrelimsPassedFinals: Preliminaries passed! Finals: go to the stadium outside the Leaf's wall{0}.
		PrelimsPassedTraining: Preliminaries passed! Get stronger before the finals (beat Skeletron, or reach {0} max life).
		FinalsPosted: Notices are up on the Leaf's streets: the Chunin Exam finals are about to begin.
		TowerReached: Heaven and Earth, opened together: the second test is passed. The proctor in the hall is waiting for you.
		FinalsAnnounce: Proctor: "Chunin Exam finals, first match: {0} versus Gaara of the Sand!"
		PrelimsAnnounce: Gekko Hayate: "(Cough.) ...Preliminaries: {0} versus Dosu of the Sound. Begin."
	}

	Handbook: {
		Title: Ninja Handbook

		Tab: {
			Mission: Mission
			Bosses: Bosses
			Jutsu: Jutsu
			Chakra: Chakra
			Rewards: Rewards
			Paths: Paths
			Lore: Records
		}

		Path: {
			Sharingan: {
				Name: Sharingan
				Ultimate: Rinnegan · Perfect Susanoo
				Teaser: Eyes that see through everything.
			}

			EightGates: {
				Name: Eight Gates
				Ultimate: Gate of Death · Night Guy
				Teaser: Youth that burns life itself.
			}

			Byakugan: {
				Name: Byakugan · Gentle Fist
				Ultimate: Tenseigan
				Teaser: Eyes that see the chakra network.
			}

			Sage: {
				Name: Sage Arts · Nine-Tails
				Ultimate: Tailed Beast Mode
				Teaser: In tune with nature and the tailed beast.
			}

			Line: - {0}: {1} Its peak: {2}
			Intro: Paths: training that crosses every class. One core at a time, each with three tiers. They light up here once you have the first tier.
			Outro: Every first tier is found between the Chunin Exams and the Destruction of the Leaf.
		}

		Progress: Progress
		AskKakashi: Not sure what to do next? Ask Kakashi.

		Wave: {
			Insignia: - Mist Insignia: {0}/3 (one from each Demon Brother, one from Tazuna when he comes clean; the Brothers still turn up in the sea mist when it rains)
			Duo: - Zabuza and Haku: {0}
			Bridge: - The seaside bridge: {0}
			Exams: - Chunin Exams: {0}
		}

		Status: {
			Defeated: defeated
			NotDefeated: not yet defeated
			NoBridge: not in this world yet (ask Kakashi for the blueprint)
			BridgeDone: finished
			BridgeBuilding: unfinished; Tazuna the bridge builder is at the bridgehead
			ExamsOpen: open
			ExamsLocked: open once Zabuza and Haku are beaten
		}

		Exam: {
			Title: Chunin Exams
			Passed: passed
			Ongoing: under way
			NotStarted: not started
			ForestFetch: under way (collect your scroll at the gate)
			ForestHunt: under way (holding the {0}; {1} squads beaten)
			Heaven: Heaven Scroll
			Earth: Earth Scroll
			Recommend: - Recommendation: {0}
			Recommended: given by Kakashi
			NotRecommended: not yet
			Written: - First test, the written test: {0}
			Forest: - Second test, the Forest of Death: {0}
			Prelims: - Preliminaries: {0}
			Finals: - Finals: {0}
			FinalsOver: over
			FinalsOpen: open
			Vow: - Your vow: {0} (once you have a style core, see the Third Hokage in the Hokage's office)
		}

		Bosses: {
			Defeated: "[Defeated] "
			NotDefeated: "[Not defeated] "
			Intro: Bosses (each can be fought again with its summoning item; the story only brings the first fight)
			Brothers: The Demon Brothers — carry a Mist Insignia into the sea mist around the bridge and they are sure to ambush you the first time; after that they may turn up when it rains. Drop Mist Insignia.
			WaveDuo: Zabuza and Haku — after the Eye of Cthulhu. Craft the Zabuza Challenge Scroll from 3 Mist Insignia and wood, and use it around the bridge. Drop class weapons, masks and a Chakra Crystal.
			Orochimaru: Orochimaru (encounter) — after the Eater of Worlds or Brain of Cthulhu (or at 300 max life). Met on the jungle surface during the second exam; afterwards, summon him on the jungle surface with a Shed Snake Skin (vines, jungle spores and stingers, at an anvil). He leaves at half life. Drops the Sharingan in a Vial (about 1 in 4).
			Dosu: Dosu Kinuta of the Sound — the preliminaries, in the central tower's hall. Afterwards, summon him in the hall with a Sound Ninja Token (iron or lead bars and Shadow Scales or Tissue Samples, at an anvil).
			Gaara: Gaara — after Skeletron (or at 400 max life). The finals, in the stadium; afterwards, summon him there with a Sand Gourd (sand and bones, at an anvil). Each character's first win always gives the Scroll of the Eight Gates and Lee's Leg Weights.
			Neji: Neji Hyuga — once the finals have begun, use the challenge Kakashi passes on to you in the stadium. Drops the Byakugan (about 1 in 4).
		}

		Jutsu: {
			Title: Substitution Jutsu (a basic jutsu, for every class)
			Logs: - You carry a few substitution logs (the log icons under the chakra bar; {0} to start)
			Auto: - When an enemy hits you hard (at least {0}% of your max life), a log is spent by itself: you swap to one side, a log drops where you stood, and the hit does nothing. No key needed. Scratches land as normal and cost no log
			Regen: - A log comes back every {0} seconds; the harder the hit it took, the longer that log takes; every hit you land brings it a little sooner
			Key: - Press [{0}] to substitute on purpose: {1} logs and {2} chakra blink you the way you are moving and hide you for {3} seconds: your next hit is a sure critical, and stronger
			Binds: - Binds like the Sand Coffin and the killing intent are always warned; dodge them and nothing happens. If one catches you, a log gets you out; without one, you are caught
			Sealed: - With three chakra points sealed, the logs are sealed too
			Drill: - To practise the timing of the key, ask Kakashi for "Substitution drill"
			Current: Now: logs {0}/{1}
		}

		Rewards: {
			Title: Land of Waves · Zabuza and Haku: {0}/{1} collected
			Weapon: - Every win gives one class weapon (one each for melee, ranged, magic and summoning), sometimes two
			Masks: - Each of the two masks drops about 1 time in 7
			FirstWin: - Each character's first win also gives a Chakra Crystal and the Wave Country Medal
			Expert: - In Expert Mode, each player gets a treasure bag instead
		}

		Lore: {
			Empty:
				'''
				Records

				(Blank.) Beat the story's bosses and their stories will be written here.
				'''
			Wave:
				'''
				Records · The Land of Waves

				[Zabuza Momochi, the Demon of the Mist] A rogue ninja of the Hidden Mist, one of the Seven Ninja Swordsmen, who carries the Executioner's Blade. They say that at the graduation exam of the Village of the Bloody Mist he killed every classmate alone, and was called the Demon ever after. When his coup failed he fled the Mist, raising money as an assassin, and Gato hired him to kill Tazuna the bridge builder.

				[Haku] A boy born with the Ice Release kekkei genkai. In the war-torn Land of Water those with kekkei genkai were hunted; Haku lost his parents, and Zabuza found him in the snow. From that day he lived only for Zabuza, content to be his "tool." On the bridge he trapped the Leaf ninja in his ice mirrors, and in the end took the killing blow meant for Zabuza.

				[Gato] A rich man who held the Land of Waves' shipping in his fist. Hearing that Zabuza had failed, he came to the bridge with hired thugs to be rid of Zabuza too, never thinking that the Demon, with Haku gone, still had one breath left in him.

				[The Bridge] Tazuna finished the bridge with the strength of the whole town. They named it the Great Naruto Bridge, after the ninja who changed their country.

				...They say the Leaf's Chunin Exams are about to begin. And that there are snakes in the Forest of Death.
				'''
		}

		Chakra: {
			Header: Chakra {0}/{1}    Chakra Crystals {2}/{3}
			Recovery: Recovery
			Natural: - Natural: {0} a second; for {1} seconds after a jutsu, {2} a second
			OnHit: - On hit: any class's attack (minions too) that hits an enemy restores {0}, at most {1} a second
			Pill: - Soldier Pill: restores {0} at once, then none for {1} seconds; a Mushroom and a Daybloom at a workbench make 2
			Raise: Raising the maximum
			Crystal: - Chakra Crystal: blue-glowing crystals in the caverns underground; mine one with a pickaxe and use it for +{0}, up to {1} before Hardmode
		}
	}

	Kakashi: {
		ButtonLesson: Lesson: {0}
		Greeting1: Yo.
		Greeting2: ...(He shuts the little orange book.) Yo.
		Greeting3: Sorry I'm late. I got lost on the road of life.
		HeardOrochimaru:
			'''
			...Hey, hey. What's with that face?

			(He hears you out, and puts the little book away.) Long hair, eyes like a snake, a neck that stretches that far... That was Orochimaru. A rogue from the Leaf. One of the Sannin, once.

			...Honestly, you're pretty lucky to be standing here. I'll report it to Lord Hokage. The exam goes on as planned. But if you see those eyes again, don't play the hero. Turn around and run.
			'''
		Handbook: Yo. Where's your Ninja Handbook? ...Here. Try not to lose it this time. Missions, jutsu, chakra, it's all in there.
		Blueprint: Yo. Tazuna the bridge builder asked me to give you this: his blueprint. There's no bridge of his on this coast yet. Use it once on the beach facing the sea to see the outline; if it looks right, use it again on the spot and up goes the bridge.
		LostRecommendation: Lost your recommendation? ...Here's another. Don't lose this one.
		NejiChallenge: That Hyuga kid, Neji, asked me to pass something on: once the finals start, he wants a match with you in the stadium. Up to you.
		NoVillage: Good work. ...We'd head back to the Leaf now, except there's no Leaf in this land. The Chunin Exams only happen in a world that has one.
		Recommendation: Yo, good work. ...Right, back to the village. Oh, and I put your name down for the Chunin Exams. Well... if you're scared, there's still time to back out.
		Says: Kakashi: {0}
		ButtonTips: Advice
		ButtonDrill: Substitution drill
		ButtonHome: Back to the village
		ButtonAcademy: To the Academy
		RideHome: Kakashi: ...Body Flicker. Here we are. Welcome back.
		RideAcademy: Kakashi: There, the Academy. The proctor's waiting for you in the classroom.
		Tip1: Substitution: you carry a few logs. When a hit really hurts, a log takes it and you're already off to one side. Scratches, you'll just have to take yourself. A log you use takes a good while to come back, and the harder the hit, the longer, so go easy on them. Press [{0}] to substitute on purpose: two logs, a flash the way you're running, you vanish, and your next strike goes for the vitals. Want to practise the timing? Pick "Substitution drill".
		Tip2: Chakra comes back on its own, slowly, and slower for a few seconds after a jutsu. Hitting enemies brings a little back too, blade, bow, magic or summons, doesn't matter.
		Tip3: A mushroom and a daybloom at a workbench make soldier pills. One gives back 40 chakra. They're for emergencies, not snacks.
		Tip4: There are blue-glowing chakra crystals in the caves underground. Like life crystals, they raise your chakra. Keep an eye out when you're mining.
		Tip5: The Mist ninja work far from the village, mostly by the sea. Get hold of their insignia and you can track down Zabuza.
		Tip6: Nobody breaks a Water Prison from the inside. If I ever get stuck in one, hit it from outside.
		Tip7: Everything I've told you is in the Ninja Handbook. Read it whenever.
		DrillStart: Watch closely—
		VowCall: Kakashi: ...Oh? So you got your hands on that. Lord Third wants to see you at the Hokage's Residence. Don't keep the old man waiting.
	}

	M0: {
		MissionSet: Mission set to {0} (tora, letter, gather, patrol; done finishes the current one)
		NinjaUsage: Usage: /m0 ninja ronin|rogue (single player only)
		NinjaSpawned: Spawned about 20 tiles ahead: {0}
		LessonSet: Kakashi's next lesson set to {0} (not started; Tazuna's confession is marked too). Ask Kakashi for the lesson.
		Usage: /m0, /m0 items, /m0 seals, /m0 tools, /m0 time <day|noon|night|midnight|hh:mm>, /m0 bridge, /m0 preview, /m0 sighting, /m0 senbon, /m0 mist, /m0 brothers, /m0 forest, /m0 squad, /m0 orochimaru, /m0 lake, /m0 story <1-5>, /m0 exam [stage|gate|tower|stadium|academy|hokage|tree|rain|rebuild], /m0 epilogue zabuza|haku [distance], /m0 cheer [boss name], /m0 ninja ronin|rogue, /m0 lesson pakkun|fireball|climbing|done, /m0 dmg [on|off], /m0 logs off|on or /m0 god [on|off]
		Description: Get the M0 test items, every item in the mod (developer wings included), or switch a temporary single-player god mode
		ItemsGiven: Gave all {0} items of the mod (developer wings included).
		ToolsGiven: Gave a shuriken and 99 paper bombs. Hold a ninja tool for about 12 seconds (quicker with ninja-tool gear); with the meter full, the next throw is a stealth throw.
		SealsGiven: Gave the three jutsu scrolls. Open your inventory and put them in the 2/4/6-seal slots right of the ammo slots; press [{0}], [{1}] and [{2}] to cast.
		NoBridge: This world has no bridge yet.
		PreviewReplayed: Replaying the mist preview here (world progress unchanged).
		LakeSingle: The lake ambush test is single player only.
		NoLake: No suitable lake on this world's surface.
		LakeStarted: Teleported to a lake ({0} tiles wide) and started the lake ambush (mission stage not checked; finishing it records LakeDone).
		StorySingle: Setting the mission stage is single player only.
		CheerQueued: Noted "beat {0}". Walk into the Leaf and the villagers will celebrate. (Teleport: /m0 exam hokage)
		OrochimaruSingle: Summoning Orochimaru's disguise is single player only.
		OrochimaruComing: The insects in the forest have suddenly gone quiet... (to count for the exam, be at the scroll hunt of the second test)
		SquadSingle: Summoning a candidate squad is single player only.
		SquadComing: A candidate squad is coming from off screen (to count, be at the scroll hunt of the second test).
		ForestSingle: Summoning the herb-gathering youth is single player only.
		ForestComing: In the woods ahead, a youth is gathering herbs.
		BrothersSingle: Summoning the Demon Brothers is single player only.
		BrothersComing: The Demon Brothers close in from both sides (Gōzu on the left, Meizu on the right).
		SightingPlayed: Playing a mist sighting here (no progress change). Near the broken end they appear in their real places; otherwise about 15 tiles ahead of you.
		SenbonPlayed: Playing a senbon warning here (no progress change). Near the broken end it comes from its real place; otherwise from about 15 tiles ahead.
		DmgOn: Damage report on: every hit you take shows its source, the table's number, the damage before and after defence, and whether a log took it. /m0 dmg again to turn it off.
		DmgOff: Damage report off.
		LogsSingle: Switching logs off is single player only.
		LogsOff: Logs off: no log takes an enemy's hit (clones still work). /m0 logs on to restore.
		LogsOn: Logs back on.
		GodSingle: Test god mode is single player only.
		GodOn: Test god mode on: all damage is ignored. /m0 god off to turn it off.
		GodOff: Test god mode off: damage is back to normal.
		EpilogueSingle: The epilogue test is single player only.
		RebuildSingle: Rebuilding the exam grounds is single player only.
		RebuildFailed: This world has no Leaf or no jungle surface; nothing to rebuild.
		Teleported: Teleported to {0}.
		NoSite: This world doesn't have that place (it needs a new world).
		NoStage: No such stage. Type /m0 exam to see the stages.
		ExamSingle: Setting the exam stage is single player only.
		TimeSingle: Changing the time is single player only.
		TimeUsage: Usage: /m0 time day (4:30) | noon (12:00) | night (19:30) | midnight (0:00) | hh:mm (24-hour)
		TimeSet: Time set to {0} ({1}).
		MistNoBridge: Sea mist check: this world has no bridge.
		Day: day
		Night: night
		BridgeTeleported: Teleported to the bridgehead. This world's bridge: {0}; the code: v{1}
		BridgeVersionUnknown: not recorded (very old)
		BridgeCurrent: .
		BridgeOutdated: ; a new world is needed to see the latest bridge and hut.
		StorySet: Mission stage set to {0} (1 find Tazuna, 2 scout, 3 back to Tazuna, 4 get stronger/lake, 5 broken bridge).
		EpilogueZabuza: Epilogue started: Zabuza speaks, then walks to Haku {0} tiles away. Kakashi appears afterwards (exam progress reset to awaiting the recommendation).
		EpilogueHaku: Epilogue started: Haku speaks, then walks to Zabuza {0} tiles away. Kakashi appears afterwards (exam progress reset to awaiting the recommendation).
		ExamStatus:
			'''
			Chunin Exams: stage {0}; grounds {1}; version v{2}/v{3}.
			Stages: {4}
			'''
		ExamNoSites: none (an old world, or no Leaf)
		Rebuilt: Rebuilt the Training Ground 44 gate, the central tower and the landmarks on the way to the new design (v{0}). The old grounds were cleared; nearby NPCs return to their posts in a few seconds.
		ExamSet: Exam stage set to {0}; it now reads as {1}.
		MistReport: Sea mist check: {0} tiles from the bridge (no mist beyond {1}); the mist is {2}; {3}; strength setting {4}; current density {5}.
		MistOn: active
		MistOff: inactive (the bridge is finished or the Land of Waves is done)
		Raining: ", raining"
	}

	Orochimaru: {
		Interesting: ...Kukuku. Your body is even more interesting than I thought. Don't go and die before we meet again.
		InterestingChat: Orochimaru: "...Kukuku. Your body is even more interesting than I thought. Don't go and die before we meet again."
		Struggle: ...How sweet you look, struggling so. The time isn't right yet. Take good care of that life until I come for it.
		StruggleChat: Orochimaru: "...How sweet you look, struggling so. The time isn't right yet. Take good care of that life until I come for it."
		Hurry: Orochimaru: "...Such haste."
		FrozenByFear: Killing intent... your body won't move!
		Left: Orochimaru breaks into a mass of snakes and burrows into the earth. Only a shed skin is left behind; use it in the jungle and he may be drawn out again.
		SkinWrongPlace: The skin still carries his scent... he can only be drawn out on the jungle surface.
	}

	Gaara: {
		Guard: Shield of Sand
		Caught: The sand has you!
		FirstWin: First win over Gaara: you get the Scroll of the Eight Gates (a style core) and Lee's Leg Weights.
		Down: Gaara falls... but the chakra pouring out of him is no longer human. Over the stadium, a genjutsu drifts down like feathers: the Destruction of the Leaf has begun. (Coming in a later update.)
		WrongPlace: Gaara is in the stadium outside the Leaf's wall. Use this on the field.
		TooEarly: It isn't your turn in the finals yet.
	}

	Neji: {
		Begin: ...Come. I'll show you what fate is.
		Rotation: Eight Trigrams Palm Rotation!
		InRange: You are within the field of my divination.
		SixtyFour: Eight Trigrams Sixty-Four Palms!
		Down: Neji: ...Isn't fate decided from the start? You've shown me... something different. (The challenge can be used again; he'll face you any time.)
		TooEarly: Neji: ...Once the finals begin, we'll meet in the stadium.
		WrongPlace: Neji is waiting in the stadium. Use this in the middle of the field.
	}

	Dosu: {
		Down: Gekko Hayate: "(Cough.) ...The winner: the Leaf candidate. Through the preliminaries." The finals will be held in a month, in the Leaf's stadium.
		WrongPlace: The preliminaries are held in the hall of the central tower in the Forest of Death. Use this in the hall.
		TooEarly: You haven't reached the preliminaries yet. Pass the second test first.
	}

	Wave: {
		Complete: Zabuza and Haku have been beaten. The Land of Waves story is complete, and the Chunin Exams are now open.
		BridgeFinished: The bridge is finished. The mist over the sea has lifted.
		AlreadyFighting: Haku or Zabuza is already here; they can't be summoned again.
		NoBridge: This world has no bridge yet. Get Tazuna's blueprint from Kakashi and build it first.
		ScrollWrongPlace: The mist has blurred the writing on the scroll... Zabuza is waiting at the broken bridge. Open it again near the bridge by the sea.
		FirstWin: First win over Zabuza and Haku: you get a Chakra Crystal and the Wave Country Medal.
	}

