	TazunaBridge: {
		Line1: I'm Tazuna, the bridge builder. Finish this bridge and the Land of Waves gets to live.
		Line2: That Gato has shut the sea lanes. No ships get in, and people can barely eat.
		Line3: Mist ninja show up when the fog rolls in, right here on the shore by the bridge.
		Line4: The bridge has stood broken off out there for ages... the workers are too scared to come.
		Line5: Every stone of this bridge was carried up there by the townsfolk, one at a time.
		Line6: There's still a stone hanging from the crane. The day the workers saw figures in the mist, they dropped everything and ran.
		Line7: My grandson Inari says there's no such thing as heroes. ...I'd like him to be wrong.
		Line8: (He takes a swig.) Ha... I may not look it, but I'm the best bridge builder in this country.
		Line9: There's a torii gate on the islet over there. The fishermen used to pray at it before they put out to sea.
		FirstMeeting: Oh? You're the ninja Kakashi brought along? I'm Tazuna, the finest bridge builder in this country. Finish this bridge and the Land of Waves gets to live... Watch yourself, though. This stretch of coast isn't safe.
		Confession:
			'''
			...The Demon Brothers? Even Mist chunin, now... I can't hide it any longer.
			I lied when I hired you. This was never a C-rank mission. Gato, the shipping magnate, wants me dead, and he's hired ninja to do it.
			Once the bridge is done, his grip on the Land of Waves is broken. But a country this poor... can't pay for an A-rank mission. Please, ninja.
			...Oh, and I found this by the hut door a few nights ago. It bears the mark of the Mist. You keep it.
			'''
		RankRaised: The mission is now A-rank. Tazuna gives you a Mist Insignia.
		Night: It's dark, and the mist is thicker. Better not go onto the bridge alone at night.
		Rain: The Mist ninja love a rainy day... be careful.
		GetStronger: Kakashi says Gato hired the Demon of the Mist... Don't push your luck. Get stronger first.
		Lake: The road to town runs past the lake... once the mist comes up there, you can't see a thing.
		Bridge: You're saying someone carried Zabuza off? ...(He goes pale.) If that man's still alive, this bridge will never be finished.
		SawPreview: You saw them too, didn't you? Those two in the mist... Gato's ninja. As long as the bridge isn't finished, they'll be waiting there.
		Insignia: Are those Mist insignia you're carrying? ...So you mean it. Please, ninja.
	}

	Tazuna: {
		Line1: The bridge is finished! All thanks to you. Want to buy something?
		Line2: Ships can come into port again, and the market's busy.
		Line3: That bridge? Everyone calls it the Great Naruto Bridge.
		Line4: Zabuza and that boy... in the end, this world drove them to it too, I suppose.
		Line5: Inari runs up onto the bridge every day now. Says he'll be a hero when he grows up.
		Line6: With Gato gone, his thugs all ran off. This country can finally breathe.
		Line7: Need wood? I've got plenty left over from the bridge.
		Line8: I hear the Leaf's holding the Chunin Exams? You're going too, aren't you? Give it your all.
		Line9: Thank that old man of the Leaf for me (the Third). I only ever paid for a C-rank mission, you know.
	}

	ToolShopkeeper: {
		Line1: Welcome! Kunai, shuriken, paper bombs: nobody in the Leaf stocks more than I do.
		Line2: Hold a tool long enough to know it, and you can hide your intent when you throw. That's what a stealth throw is.
		Line3: Don't run around with paper bombs in your shirt. Stick one in the wrong place and it's no joke.
		Line4: My girl Tenten keeps going on about becoming a ninja like Lady Tsunade.
		Line5: Shuriken bounce off walls. Get the angle right and you can hit someone behind one.
		AfterWave: I hear you brought Mist senbon back from the Land of Waves? I've got a batch in, not much worse than the ones that Haku used.
		AfterExams: Well done at the Chunin Exams! Tenten says she saw you in the stadium. I'll have her help out in the shop.
	}

	HakuForest: {
		Line1: Good morning. Are you... from around here? I'm gathering herbs. The plants in this forest are good for healing wounds.
		Line2: There is someone very precious to me. For him, I would do anything.
		Line3: Do you have someone precious? ...A person only becomes truly strong when they have someone they want to protect.
		Line4: You will become strong. Perhaps... we will meet again.
		Parting: Oh, and— I'm a boy.
		Continue: Continue
		Farewell: Say goodbye
	}

	Ibiki: {
		GaveUp: You gave up once. Don't come back today. Think it over and come at dawn.
		NoRecommendation: Where's your recommendation? Nobody enters this room without a jonin's say-so. Go and find your squad leader.
		Welcome:
			'''
			I am the proctor of the first test, Morino Ibiki.

			There is one rule: get caught cheating more than once and you're out on the spot. ...Sit down when you're ready.
			'''
		NotYet: ...This is a Chunin Exam room. It isn't your turn yet.
		Passed: You've passed the first test. The Forest of Death is far more dangerous than this classroom. Don't die.
		ButtonStart: Begin the test
		Begin: —Begin!
	}

