		TenthIntro:
			'''
			Morino Ibiki: "Before the tenth question, the rules.

			You may choose not to take it. Give up, and your exam ends here.
			Take it, and get it wrong... and you will never sit the Chunin Exams again as long as you live."
			'''
		TenthAccepted:
			'''
			Morino Ibiki: "...Good. You pass.

			The tenth question was whether you would take it at all. As a chunin you will lead a squad into missions whose outcome no one knows.
			Those who cannot step forward then have no right to be chunin."
			'''
		TenthGaveUp:
			'''
			Morino Ibiki: "Knowing when to pull back is a judgement too. ...But today, you are done.

			Come back at dawn, once you've thought it over."
			'''
		LeftRoom: You left the exam room. You can start the written test again any time.
		Header: Chunin Exams · First Test    Question {0} / 10
		HeaderTenth: Chunin Exams · First Test    Question 10
		HeaderEnd: Chunin Exams · First Test
		Accept: Take the tenth question
		GiveUp: Give up
		GaveUpNote: You gave up on the tenth question. You can sit the test again after the next dawn.
		Leave: Leave the room
	}

	Iruka: {
		Line1: I'm Iruka. I teach at the Ninja Academy and help out at the mission desk in the Hokage's Residence.
		Line2: D-rank missions don't look like much, but they're what keep the village running.
		Line3: Tora's run off again? ...The Fire Daimyo's wife's cat gets lost a few times a year.
		Line4: Save up your mission tokens and you can trade them with me for blueprints and chakra pills.
		Line5: Whatever rank you reach, don't forget what you learned at the Academy.
		AfterWave: That Land of Waves mission was only supposed to be C-rank, wasn't it? I'm glad you all came back safe.
		TakeMission: Take a mission
		ReportMission: Mission
		Exchange: Exchange
	}

	Mission: {
		Taken: Mission accepted: {0}
		Complete: Mission complete: {0}. Report back to Iruka at the Hokage's Residence.
		ReportBack: Done already? Well done! Tell me how it went.
		Paid: Good work! Here's your pay: {0} silver and {1} mission tokens. Ready for the next one?

		Tora: {
			Name: Find Tora the Lost Cat
			Brief: Tora again... the Daimyo's wife's cat has run off. She has a ribbon on her right ear. She bolts when you get close; chase her down and touch her to catch her.
			Task: Find Tora and catch her.
			Direction: Someone saw Tora heading {0}, somewhere on the surface a hundred or two tiles out.
			Caught: Caught Tora!
		}

		Letter: {
			Name: Deliver a Letter
			Brief: There's a letter to deliver. Put it in the addressee's hands; just talk to them.
			Task: Deliver the letter to {0}.
		}

		Gather: {
			Name: Gathering
			Brief: The village needs some supplies. Bring them back to me.
			Task: Bring back {0} {1} (you have {2}).
		}

		Patrol: {
			Name: Night Patrol
			Brief: Gato's ronin have been prowling outside the village at night. Go on patrol and take them down.
			Task: Defeat {0} of Gato's ronin outside the village at night ({1} so far).
		}
	}

	Lesson: {
		AllDone: That's all I've got to teach you. The rest you learn by fighting. ...Well, drop by for substitution drills if you're bored.

		Pakkun: {
			Name: Find Pakkun
			Start: Summoning, huh... First you need an animal willing to sign a contract with you. Mine's called Pakkun. Great nose, stubborn temper. He caught a scent a minute ago and took off. Bring him back; if he takes to you, he'll lend you a paw.
			Remind: Pakkun? Still not found him? He can't have gone far... probably. Search the surface.
			Direction: Kakashi: Pakkun's scent heads {0}, a hundred or two tiles off.
			Done: Pakkun: "Yo. Kakashi sent you? ...Fine, I'll sign. Call me when you need a nose." (Learned Summoning: Ninken)
		}

		Fireball: {
			Name: The Great Fireball
			Start: This one's the Uchiha clan's coming-of-age test. Not that you're an Uchiha. Find a lake, stand on the shore, and breathe it out over the water with the 4-seal key [{0}]. It only counts once the fireball covers the water.
			Remind: At a lake, [{0}], over the water. ...Not at me.
			Try1: Pff... just a puff of smoke
			Try2: Bigger. Not enough yet!
			Try3: Fire Style: Great Fireball Jutsu!
			Done: Kakashi: ...Oh, you actually did it. Here's the scroll; it goes in your 4-seal slot.
		}

		Climbing: {
			Name: Tree Climbing
			Start: This lesson is the dullest and the most useful: gather chakra in your feet and run straight up a wall. Find a tall one (the Leaf's walls will do), jump on, cling, hold up or toward the wall, and run 15 tiles in one go. Run short of chakra and you'll slide down; jump to kick off the wall.
			Remind: The wall's still there. Cling on and run up 15 tiles. ...Slide down and you just try again.
			Done: Kakashi: Mm, a pass. From now on you can run up walls. Just don't go climbing into other people's yards. (Learned chakra wall-walking)
		}
	}

	Loadout: {
		Short: {
			Brothers: Demon Brothers
			EyeOfCthulhu: Eye of Cthulhu
			Lake: Water Prison
			WaveDuo: Zabuza & Haku
			EvilBoss: EoW / BoC
			Orochimaru: Orochimaru
			Dosu: Dosu
			QueenBee: Queen Bee
			Skeletron: Skeletron
			Neji: Neji
			Gaara: Gaara
		}

		Title: Recommended loadout (not the only way; vanilla alternatives in brackets)
		Melee: Taijutsu / Blade
		Tools: Ninja Tools
		Ninjutsu: Ninjutsu
		Summon: Summoning
		Common: For everyone
		Tactics: How to fight
		Line: - {0}: {1}
		Planned: " (planned)"

		Intro: {
			EyeOfCthulhu: Eye of Cthulhu (vanilla) — summoned at night with a Suspicious Looking Eye, or comes by itself once you are strong enough.
			Lake: The water prison at the lake — after Tazuna comes clean, once the Eye of Cthulhu is down or at 200 max life, at a surface lake.
			EvilBoss: Eater of Worlds / Brain of Cthulhu (vanilla) — break three hearts or orbs in the Corruption or Crimson, or use its summoning item.
			QueenBee: Queen Bee (vanilla) — break the larva in an underground jungle hive, or use an Abeemination.
			Skeletron: Skeletron (vanilla) — talk to the old man at the Dungeon's door at night.
		}

		Brothers: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (copper, tin armor) · Training Ninjato (Platinum Broadsword, Enchanted Sword) · Training Post
			Tools: Genin Combat Gear · kunai, shuriken + paper bombs · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Academy Training Gear · Phoenix Sage Fire (Wand of Sparking) · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear · Ninken (Finch Staff)
			Common: Clone Jutsu; Leaf Headband
			Tactics: They pincer you from both sides; when the chain flashes taut, jump it. When one falls the other goes berserk, so keep a log in hand.
		}

		EyeOfCthulhu: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (gold, platinum armor) · Training Ninjato, Chain Gauntlet (Enchanted Sword) · Training Post
			Tools: Genin Combat Gear · shuriken (they bounce; good with platforms) + paper bombs · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Academy Training Gear · Phoenix Sage Fire (Wand of Sparking, Amethyst Staff) · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear · Ninken (Finch Staff)
			Common: Great Fireball (bursts at once on a large enemy)
			Tactics: The usual: build a platform arena and dodge the dashes.
		}

		Lake: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear · Training Ninjato (the arc cuts several water clones) · Training Post
			Tools: Genin Combat Gear · shuriken · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Academy Training Gear · Phoenix Sage Fire (the spread clears clones) · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear · Ninken
			Common: Clone Jutsu
			Tactics: The prison breaks only from outside; the water clones reform, so clear them as you hit the prison.
		}

		WaveDuo: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (an extra log for the dashes; platinum armor) · Training Ninjato, Chain Gauntlet (Enchanted Sword, Blade of Grass) · Training Post
			Tools: Genin Combat Gear (stealth throws of three kunai) · kunai + paper bombs (stick them on Zabuza) · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Academy Training Gear · Phoenix Sage Fire + Great Fireball (Zabuza is big, so it bursts at once) · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear · Ninken (Finch Staff, Slime Staff)
			Common: Clone Jutsu takes the senbon from the ice mirrors
			Tactics: Break 4 mirrors to end the ice-mirror cage early; the dash in the mist is warned 0.4 s ahead; beating Haku first is easier (frenzied Zabuza takes 25% more damage).
		}

		EvilBoss: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (platinum armor) · Executioner's Blade (Enchanted Sword) · Training Post
			Tools: Mist Hunter Gear (planned) (Genin Combat Gear) · senbon (they pierce, good on worm segments) + paper bombs · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Academy Training Gear (meteor armor) · Water Dragon (Vilethorn, Space Gun) · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear (Flinx Fur Coat) · Demonic Ice Mirrors + Ninken (Flinx Staff)
			Common: Clone Jutsu, Great Fireball
			Tactics: The usual.
		}

		Orochimaru: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (shadow, crimson armor) · Executioner's Blade (Light's Bane, Blood Butcherer) · Training Post
			Tools: Mist Hunter Gear (planned) (Genin Combat Gear) · senbon + paper bombs · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Academy Training Gear (meteor armor) · Water Dragon (Vilethorn, Space Gun) · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear (Flinx Fur Coat) · Demonic Ice Mirrors + Ninken
			Common: Clone Jutsu (takes the killing intent and the snake hands)
			Tactics: The killing intent is a red wedge: leave it or get behind a wall within a second; the neck bite and the Kusanagi show where they aim; he leaves at half life or when you hold out, and falling counts too.
		}

		Dosu: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (shadow, crimson armor) · Executioner's Blade (Light's Bane, Blood Butcherer) · Training Post
			Tools: Mist Hunter Gear (planned) (Genin Combat Gear) · senbon, shuriken (kite him; stay out of reach) · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Academy Training Gear (meteor armor) · Water Dragon · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear · Demonic Ice Mirrors + Ninken
			Common: Clone Jutsu
			Tactics: The Echo Drill swaps left and right for about 2 seconds; only the outer edge of the resonance ring hurts, so inside it is safe; past half life he attacks faster.
		}

		QueenBee: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (shadow, crimson armor) · Executioner's Blade (Blade of Grass) · Training Post
			Tools: Mist Hunter Gear (planned) · senbon (pierce the little bees) · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Chakra Training Gear (planned) (jungle armor) · Water Dragon · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear · Demonic Ice Mirrors + Ninken
			Common: Clone Jutsu, Great Fireball
			Tactics: The usual.
		}

		Skeletron: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (shadow, crimson armor) · Executioner's Blade (Light's Bane, Bee Keeper) · Training Post
			Tools: Mist Hunter Gear (planned) · senbon + paper bombs · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Chakra Training Gear (planned) (jungle armor) · Water Dragon (Bee Gun) · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear (bee armor) · Demonic Ice Mirrors (Hornet Staff)
			Common: Clone Jutsu, Great Fireball
			Tactics: The usual.
		}

		Neji: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (shadow, crimson armor) · Executioner's Blade (his Gentle Fist seals you up close; melee is risky) · Training Post
			Tools: Mist Hunter Gear (planned) · senbon, shuriken · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Chakra Training Gear (planned) (jungle armor) · Water Dragon · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear · Demonic Ice Mirrors
			Common: Clone Jutsu
			Tactics: Ranged is easiest: the Gentle Fist works only up close, and three sealed points lock your logs and seals; Rotation knocks projectiles away, so wait it out; step out of the circle the moment Sixty-Four Palms marks it.
		}

		Gaara: {
			Melee: Academy Training Gear (shadow, crimson armor) · Executioner's Blade (Bee Keeper); dash round behind him · Training Post
			Tools: Mist Hunter Gear (planned) · shuriken (bounce them in from the side) + paper bombs · Ninja Tool Pouch
			Ninjutsu: Chakra Training Gear (planned) (jungle armor) · Water Dragon · Soldier Pill Pouch
			Summon: Academy Training Gear (bee armor) · Demonic Ice Mirrors + Ninken (minions go round behind)
			Common: Clone Jutsu or a log takes the Sand Coffin
			Tactics: While his sand wall is up, the front takes a tenth of the damage: get behind him or wait for the 2 seconds he spends catching his breath; quicksand marks blink before the pillars rise, so stand between two; once he transforms there are no more walls, only wide sand arms and air bullets.
		}
	}
}
